iting extraction of those data. To avoid fabrication, the present audit replays the exact historical v0.7 Genesis simulation source and applies a target-independent peak definition: a node is a peak only when its absolute amplitude exceeds all six lattice neighbors, with no threshold and no forced peak count. At the final replayed state, 304 strict peaks are found. The A2A^2 rank branch reaches R2≈0.9113R^2\approx0.9113 but has spacing CV ≈2.9682\approx2.9682, demonstrating that a superficially linear rank plot does not imply quantization. The quartic A4A^4 branch gives R2≈0.6048R^2\approx0.6048 and spacing CV ≈5.0408\approx5.0408. Across the full historical snapshot schedule, the quartic branch never approaches the historical CV<0.3 rigidity control. The BQ-R1 additive quartic-cycle candidate therefore fails in this first untuned historical-simulation realization. This does not globally falsify BQ-R1 because local maxima are not the missing v0.3 cluster segmentation and the candidate’s boundary-excitation observable has not been independently derived. It does, however, prevent retrofitting BQ-R1 onto historical v0.7 peaks after exposure. Physical promotion remains zero.

