OUT NECESSARY FOR CHIRAL LAW Physical promotion: 0 0. Question Does variance correction make the scalar quadratic calorimeter sufficient to test a signed or chiral winding-response law? Ruling: no. Variance correction removes the second-moment contamination but cannot recover information that the observation map destroyed before averaging. 1. Quadratic observation quotient Let winding live in a real or complex inner-product space. A scalar calorimeter has the form O2(w)=β∥w∥2. O_2(w)= eta\|w\|^2. Therefore O2(−w)=O2(w).  oxed{O_2(-w)=O_2(w).} More generally, O2(Uw)=O2(w) O_2(Uw)=O_2(w) for every norm-preserving orthogonal/unitary transformation UU. Thus one scalar quadratic datum identifies an entire equal-norm orbit rather than one winding state. For real dd-component winding the nonzero observation fiber is a sphere S∥w∥d−1. S^{d-1}_{\|w\|}. In particular, opposite chiralities ww and −w-w are exactly indistinguishable. AUTO_LOCK QUADRATIC_SCALAR_WINDING_OBSERVATION_FACTORS_THROUGH_NORM_AND_IS_BLIND_TO_SIGN_THEOREM_v0.1 2. Exact chiral-mixture test Consider the minimal chiral source w={+μ,probability p,−μ,probability 1−p, w=  egin{cases} +\mu,&	ext{probability }p,\ -\mu,&	ext{probability }1-p, \end{cases} plus zero-mean additive noise of variance σ2\sigma^2. Then 𝔼[w]=(2p−1)μ.  oxed{\mathbb E[w]=(2p-1)\mu.} But the quadratic mean is 𝔼[w2]=μ2+σ2,  oxed{\mathbb E[w^2]=\mu^2+\sigma^2,} which is completely independent of pp. The variance is Var(w)=μ2+σ2−(2p−1)2μ2. \operatorname{Var}(w) = \mu^2+\sigma^2-(2p-1)^2\mu^2. Subtracting it gives 𝔼[w2]−Var(w)=(2p−1)2μ2=|𝔼w|2.  oxed{ \mathbb E[w^2]-\operatorname{Var}(w) = (2p-1)^2\mu^2 = |\mathbb E w|^2. } This is still invariant under p↔1−p, p\leftrightarrow1-p, which reverses chirality. Thus variance correction recovers the magnitude of the mean winding, not its sign. AUTO_LOCK VARIANCE_CORRECTED_QUADRATIC_WINDING_READOUT_REMAINS_CHIRALITY_BLIND_THEOREM_v0.1 3. Linear readout For a source-declared analyzer aa, O1(w)=⟨a,w⟩. O_1(w)=\langle a,wangle. Then 𝔼[O1]=⟨a,𝔼w⟩.  oxed{ \mathbb E[O_1] = \langle a,\mathbb E wangle. } For the chiral mixture, 𝔼[O1]=(2p−1)⟨a,μ⟩.  oxed{ \mathbb E[O_1] = (2p-1)\langle a,\muangle. } Under chirality reversal, p↔1−p, p\leftrightarrow1-p, the result changes sign. Therefore a linear analyzer with ⟨a,μ⟩≠0 \langle a,\muangle
eq0 contains signed chirality information that no scalar norm-squared measurement can recover. AUTO_LOCK LINEAR_WINDING_ANALYZER_PRESERVES_SIGNED_CHIRALITY_COMPONENT_THEOREM_v0.1 4. Complex/phase winding If w=eiϕμ, w=e^{i\phi}\mu, then |w|2=|μ|2 |w|^2=|\mu|^2 is independent of ϕ\phi. A complex linear projection gives ⟨a,w⟩=eiϕ⟨a,μ⟩. \langle a,wangle = e^{i\phi}\langle a,\muangle. Thus a phase-sensitive constellation readout can retain phase/chirality information. If the apparatus returns only one real quadrature, it preserves only one projected component. Full complex phase recovery requires two independent quadratures or an equivalent spanning constellation. 5. Necessity criterion The scalar calorimeter is fundamentally insufficient whenever the law under test is odd or chiral, for example R(−w)=−R(w) R(-w)=-R(w) or the law is explicitly linear in signed winding: R(w)=⟨a,w⟩. R(w)=\langle a,wangle. No number of calorimetric repetitions repairs this structural non-identifiability. A phase/sign-sensitive linear observation is therefore necessary for direct testing of such a law. By contrast, if the source law is proven independently to be achiral/even, R(−w)=R(w), R(-w)=R(w), and depends only on a norm or second moment, then the scalar calorimeter may be sufficient after the variance-curvature correction. AUTO_LOCK — CONDITIONAL NECESSITY LINEAR_CONSTELLATION_READOUT_IS_NECESSARY_FOR_DIRECT_TEST_OF_SIGNED_OR_CHIRAL_WINDING_RESPONSE_v0.1 6. Consequence for §7.26 The observation-map declaration must distinguish two questions: Quadratic calorimeter Tests an even, magnitude-like response after D2(Var) D_2(\operatorname{Var}) subtraction. It cannot validate the sign/chirality of a linear winding law. Linear constellation/curl readout Tests the response in the same functional class in which a linear signed-winding law is written. It also avoids the quadratic variance term because expectation commutes with the linear map. Therefore the constellation readout is: merely cleaner if the independently established source law is achiral/even; necessary if the source law is signed/chiral. The open empirical/theoretical question is therefore not whether the calorimeter has enough precision. It is whether the source law is chirality-sensitive. Physical promotion remains 0.

